==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{m|non|skítr}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*skītaz}}. Compare Danish {{m|da|skide}}, Icelandic {{m|is|skítur}}, Dutch {{m|nl|schijt}}, English {{m|en|shit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Sv-skit.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}
* {{IPA|/ˈɧiːt/|lang=sv}}

===Noun===
{{head|sv|noun|g=c}}

# {{lb|sv|strongly colloquial}} [[excrement]]; [[shit]]
#: ''Det är '''skit''' på mattan.'' "There's shit on the carpet."
# {{lb|sv|strongly colloquial}} dirt, filth
#: ''Ta bort den där '''skiten''' från skrivbordet.'' "Get that crap off the desk."
# {{lb|sv|strongly colloquial}} someone or something undesirable or revolting
#: ''Jag börjar tröttna på den här '''skiten'''.'' "I'm getting tired of this shit."
#: ''Du är bara en liten '''skit'''.'' "You're just a little shit."
# {{lb|sv|strongly colloquial}} ''as the first part of compound used to indicate something negative''
#: ''Det här är ett jävla '''skitjobb'''.'' "This is a damned crappy job."
# {{lb|sv|strongly colloquial}} ''as the first part of compound used to intensify the positive or negative aspect of something''
#: ''Den där filmen var '''skitbra'''.'' "That movie was really good."
#: ''De lagar '''skitgod''' mat.'' "They cook really good food."

